{
  "AC": "A large todo (todo:d56d) opens with Body and Work items collapsed, showing a size hint, and every small todo renders as it does today. An oversized work-item summary clamps with a working inline expander that does not trigger the fold. A permalink to an objid inside a collapsed section renders the page with that section open and the target marked; focusing never closes an open section, and focusing twice is idempotent. Existing permalink, objid and render tests stay green.",
  "ActualSummary": "Landed as planned in three code items plus a doc item the plan missed. Sections collapse into native <details> when oversized (two triggers: content chars and item count) and box summaries clamp behind a '...more' expander; a section holding the permalink target renders open, decided server-side rather than from JS, so it is testable and has no flash. The plan's last item was a LOCAP verify, which invariant #6 refuses as a final node -- so verification became a checkpoint and the SKILL.md permalink-table update, genuinely required by the behavior change, became the closing commit. Verification found the real culprit was not Body (already capped at 20vh by CSS) but the uncapped work-item boxes; on todo:d56d 17 of 19 boxes now clamp, and 33 of the 64 todos in the store render byte-identical to before.",
  "BaseSha": "db476196c6b46fd3ac9a6b9f1eb311e7f254834e",
