    "objid": "0002",
    "raw": "PROBLEM: todo_web renders every field at full length, so a big todo is unreadable.\nOn todo:d56d the Body is ~1400 lines of ratified design, and the work-item boxes are\nfull-screen-tall each because their summaries are 500-char paragraphs -- the boxes row\nscrolls off the screen as a wall of near-empty columns before Subtodos is reachable.\nThe viewer is otherwise the right shape; nothing here changes what is rendered, only how\nmuch of it is on screen at once.\n\nRATIFIED (2026-08-08, with the user):\n1. BOTH levels collapse. Sections (Body, Long summary, State, Work items, Subtodos,\n   Fields) get a header toggle; AND an individual work-item / subtodo box whose summary is\n   oversized clamps to a few lines with its own inline expander.\n2. Collapsed ONLY when large. A section under the size threshold renders exactly as it\n   does today -- no toggle churn, no extra click, on the many small todos. Over it, the\n   section starts collapsed and its header carries a size hint (line count for prose, item\n   count for a list).\n3. Thresholds live in named module constants so they can be tuned in one place.\n4. FOCUS OPENS, NEVER CLOSES. A permalink (/<todoid>/objid/<objid>, or any deeper path)\n   whose target sits inside a collapsed section or a clamped box must OPEN every collapsing\n   ancestor on the way in, then scroll to and mark the target as it does today. It must\n   never collapse anything that is already open, and re-focusing must be idempotent.\n   This is the one rule with teeth: the permalink contract is \"the path IS the resource,\n   this todo focused here\", and a target hidden inside a closed box breaks it silently.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION NOTES:\n- Prefer native <details>/<summary> for the section toggle: free keyboard and click\n  handling, and focus-opens is then just setting .open = true on ancestors. No new\n  client state machine.\n- The work-item box already has a click handler that opens the fold. An inline expander\n  inside the box MUST stop propagation, or expanding the text also swaps the fold.\n- Selection stays objid-keyed (one data-obj over DATA.objects). Collapsing must not\n  introduce any positional or id-based client lookup -- see _box_attrs.\n- The static rendition used in the fold (interactive=False) should not grow toggles; it\n  is a read-only repr of another todo.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: persisting open/closed state across page loads; collapsing the fold itself;\nany change to what the record contains or to the permalink grammar."
  },
