      "message": "feat(todo-web): collapse an oversized section into <details>\n\nA big todo was unreadable: d56d's Body alone is 200+ lines of ratified design\nand pushes everything after it off the screen.\n\n_section() now builds every section (Summary, Long summary, Body, State,\nParent, Work items, Subtodos, Fields) and wraps it in native <details> when\nthe CONTENT is oversized -- measured on the source text, never the rendered\nmarkup, which would scale with box count and collapse a short list for the\nwrong reason. Two triggers, _COLLAPSE_CHARS and _COLLAPSE_ITEMS: twenty short\nboxes wrap into as much screen as one long one. Under both, a section renders\nbyte-identical to before, so small todos gain no toggle and no extra click.\n\nNative <details> over a bespoke toggle: it brings its own keyboard and click\nhandling, and \"open the section holding the permalink target\" becomes one\nattribute the server sets (next work item). The fold's static repr of another\ntodo never grows toggles.\n\ntests: test_todo_web_render.py SectionCollapseTest -- oversized body collapses\nwith a line count, small body unchanged, item-count trigger fires on its own,\nlong state note collapses, singular hint, static repr untouched. Line count\nrstrips the trailing newline (200 lines, not 201).",
      "objid": "0007",
      "sha": "0c986ceb0885f9f93c25fc09f8c0255623d350ca",
      "summary": "[MIDCAP] Section collapsing. Measure each rendered section's size server-side and wrap an OVERSIZED one in native <details> (closed) with a size hint in the <summary> header -- line count for prose, item count for a list. A section under the threshold renders byte-identical to today: no <details>, no toggle. Thresholds go in named module constants next to _DEDICATED_FIELDS. Applies to Body, Long summary, State, Work items, Subtodos and the generic Fields rows; the static fold rendition (interactive=False) never grows toggles. Tests: large section collapses with a hint, small one is unchanged, static repr unaffected."
