      "message": "feat(todo-web): clamp an oversized box summary behind an inline expander\n\nA groomed work item states its own acceptance criteria, so its summary is\nroutinely a 500-char paragraph -- and one of those makes a box taller than the\nscreen, turning the row of boxes into a column of walls with no overview left.\n\n_clamped() caps the height of any box summary over _CLAMP_CHARS (work items,\nsubtodos, parents alike) and adds a \"...more\" toggle. The full text stays in\nthe DOM, so browser find and copy still reach all of it; only the height is\ncapped, via CSS line-clamp.\n\nThe expander stops propagation for the same reason .idlink already does: the\nenclosing box's click opens the fold, and asking to read more of a summary is\nnot asking for that. Static boxes in the fold get neither clamp nor button --\nthey are a read-only repr, not a page you interact with.\n\ntests: test_todo_web_render.py BoxClampTest -- paragraph clamps and keeps its\nfull text, short summary renders exactly as before, handler stops propagation,\nstatic repr stays plain. Assertions scope to the #top markup, since the\nstylesheet and script name every class the page can ever use.",
