      "message": "feat(todo-web): a collapsed section renders open when it holds the focus target\n\nCollapsing introduced a way for a permalink to hide its own target: link to\n/<todoid>/objid/<objid> for a work item, and the Work items section is closed\non arrival because it is oversized -- the page scrolls to a box nobody can see.\n\nThe server already resolves focus_objid before rendering, so the decision is\nmade there rather than opened from JS after load: directly testable, works with\nJS off, and no flash of collapsed content. _holds() asks whether the focus\nobjid is anywhere inside a section's value (recursing, so an undrawn nested\nobject still opens the section its box lives in), and only ever forces open.\n\nFocus never closes: a section under the threshold has no <details> to shut, a\nsibling section stays as it was, and re-rendering the same permalink produces a\nbyte-identical page.\n\ntests: test_todo_web_render.py FocusOpensTest -- holding section opens, same\nsection closed without focus, siblings unaffected, a section-field target opens\nits own section, idempotent re-render, unknown objid opens nothing, and _holds\nis false with no target at all.\n\nFull suite: 502 passed.",
